              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JennB1972"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Here's a thought for all the negative-nancy types though...If you don't like salt, lemon or garlic--hmmm. Maybe don't TRY a GARLIC LEMON SEA SALT dish?? Just sayin'! ;o)"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Scotdog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I can't quit eating these! I had no idea you could cook broccoli this way. It is SO good! Thanks! Update since some found this salty - I never use salt in any recipe (except breadmaker). These are really tasty. If you fear the lemon might be too strong, use less the first time.",
            "datePublished": "2008-07-04T19:14:59.697Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Victoria Schano"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I actually had a suggestion for anyone of you who loves garlic! This recipe is so simple but for flavor. Instead of using plain garlic, I use roasted garlic. Take a garlic bowl cut the tops off and wrap it in aluminum foil place in the oven at about 400° for about 20 minutes. When you used oven baked garlic it's a little on the sweeter side and goes very nicely with the way the broccoli caramelizes in the oven. If you like garlic that is. Everything else was perfect and this is the best recipe I have found so far! I didn't make any changes except leaving the broccoli to cook for five min more, I like mine well done",
            "datePublished": "2021-03-20T02:41:07.980Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Ann B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very tasty. I made some modifications as follows: I used garlic flavored olive oil. Since I never have garlic in the house, I used minced garlic from the jar, and a lot of it. It was going in the oven with something else which was set at 375 deg, so it was in for 30 min and was perfect. At the end, I sprinkled it with lemon juice and grated parmesan-reggiano cheese. Hubby loved it. This is a keeper.",
            "datePublished": "2021-01-21T00:56:53.950Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Needed a good vegetable for a spur of the moment dinner and the only thing I had was a bag of frozen broccoli! This recipe sounded so good that I defrosted the broccoli (microwaved slightly until it was no longer frozen, but still firm) and then made this recipe. The only other change I made was that I had two fresh sweet Italian red peppers, which I sliced and added. Now this is my favorite broccoli recipe. Loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-17T11:29:07.127Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patricia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn’t toss the broccoli and olive oil but drizzled the olive oil over the florets. Instead of minced garlic, I sprinkled garlic powder on it (a fair amount as we like garlic). In addition to lemon juice, I sprinkled with lemon zest. I forgot the pepper but added it at the table to taste.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-11T00:35:26.830Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I could have just eaten this for dinner tonight! I too was nervous about the small amount of evoo but was perfect. I used pink Himalayan salt and an extra couple garlic cloves minced. I let sit in the bowl, “marinating” while I finished my other dishes/meal prep. Cooked 15 min @ 400 was perfect in my oven. The splash of lemon juice? Bites of roasted garlic with the broccoli? Divine!! Thanks for an easy yet wonderful side dish!",
            "datePublished": "2022-02-11T03:59:31.972Z"
